    <p class="lead" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="150">In Acts 18:27, the Apostle Paul refers to Apollos as someone who “proved to be a great benefit (or advantage)” to the early church. As the name implies, our heart is to be an advantage to church leaders across Pennsylvania.</p>
